{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:91a46d65b25313a3a2b70a7e34e71969141b82a30901c5a6a5116d40ed992e23","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Modularity-of-elliptic-curves-over-imaginary-quadratic-fields-October-4-2026#thm:main","title":"thm:main"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/410b6217df874144fdba0cfc.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","generation_id":"sha256:c701139844a2d825c371ded7486924e7dae7de0af77a69dc9c1abaf1129191a1","id":"r:Modularity-of-elliptic-curves-over-imaginary-quadratic-fields-October-4-2026:thm:main","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Modularity-of-elliptic-curves-over-imaginary-quadratic-fields-October-4-2026","name":"thm:main","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":"1.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","binding":{"file":"build/sections/introduction.tex","label":"thm:main","line":17,"manuscript":"Modularity-of-elliptic-curves-over-imaginary-quadratic-fields-October-4-2026","statement_sha256":"68d87376b3f3140370d702f8324b15aa87ab9147a41294b9175aa9bfb78a2337"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Modularity-of-elliptic-curves-over-imaginary-quadratic-fields-October-4-2026.html#thm:main","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:493700624a2656ff1c2e8b45c5c2494508b28b4d9db2621c5fd0aa25d8246391","file":"preprints/Modularity-of-elliptic-curves-over-imaginary-quadratic-fields-October-4-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":17,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"68d87376b3f3140370d702f8324b15aa87ab9147a41294b9175aa9bfb78a2337","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Modularity-of-elliptic-curves-over-imaginary-quadratic-fields-October-4-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:493700624a2656ff1c2e8b45c5c2494508b28b4d9db2621c5fd0aa25d8246391","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Modularity-of-elliptic-curves-over-imaginary-quadratic-fields-October-4-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L17"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $K$ be an imaginary quadratic number field and $E/K$ an elliptic\ncurve. There is an isobaric automorphic representation $\\pi_E$ of\n$\\GL_2(\\A_K)$ with trivial central character and weight zero such that,\nfor every prime $l$ and every isomorphism\n$\\iota:\\overline\\Q_l\\xrightarrow{\\sim}\\C$,\n\\[\n r_\\iota(\\pi_E)\\simeq\n H^1_{\\et}(E_{\\overline K},\\overline\\Q_l).\n\\]\nAt every finite place $v\\nmid l$ one has\n\\[\n \\iota\\WD\\bigl(H^1_{\\et}(E_{\\overline K},\\overline\\Q_l)\n                     |_{G_{K_v}}\\bigr)^{\\Fss}\n \\simeq\n \\rec_{K_v}\\bigl(\\pi_{E,v}\\otimes|\\det|_v^{-1/2}\\bigr).\n\\]\nThe unitary parameter at the complex place is\n$z\\mapsto\\diag(z/|z|,\\overline z/|z|)$.\nIn particular every local factor agrees, and\n\\[\n L(E/K,s)=L(\\pi_E,s-1/2).\n\\]\nIf $E$ has no complex multiplication, $\\pi_E$ is cuspidal. In the CM\ncase it is given by automorphic induction of a Hecke character, or by\nan isobaric sum when the CM field is already $K$."}
